    <Member MemberName="WebSocketKeepAliveInterval">
      <MemberSignature Language="C#" Value="public static TimeSpan WebSocketKeepAliveInterval { get; }" />
      <MemberSignature Language="ILAsm" Value=".property valuetype System.TimeSpan WebSocketKeepAliveInterval" />
      <MemberSignature Language="DocId" Value="P:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.FoundryEnvironment.WebSocketKeepAliveInterval" />
      <MemberSignature Language="VB.NET" Value="Public Shared ReadOnly Property WebSocketKeepAliveInterval As TimeSpan" />
      <MemberSignature Language="F#" Value="static member WebSocketKeepAliveInterval : TimeSpan" Usage="Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.FoundryEnvironment.WebSocketKeepAliveInterval" />
      <MemberType>Property</MemberType>
      <AssemblyInfo>
        <AssemblyName>Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core</AssemblyName>
        <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
      </AssemblyInfo>
      <ReturnValue>
        <ReturnType>System.TimeSpan</ReturnType>
      </ReturnValue>
      <Docs>
        <summary>
            The WebSocket Ping/Pong keep-alive interval used by the
            <c>invocations_ws</c> protocol. Sourced from the <c>WS_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL</c>
            environment variable (value in integer seconds). When absent, zero, or
            unparseable, returns <see cref="F:System.Threading.Timeout.InfiniteTimeSpan" /> (disabled —
            Kestrel default of 30s does <em>not</em> apply because Core sets the
            option explicitly to honour the spec's "disabled by default" contract).
            </summary>
        <value>To be added.</value>
        <remarks>
            Wired into ASP.NET Core's <c>WebSocketOptions.KeepAliveInterval</c> so a
            positive value emits RFC 6455 protocol-level Ping frames (opcode
            <c>0x9</c>) at the configured cadence. The Foundry hosting platform
            auto-injects this env var; configure it locally to test long-lived WS
            connections through upstream proxy / load-balancer idle timeouts.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
